<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n36119" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Phoebus</span></b> , i, m., =
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Φοῖβος</span> (the radiant), <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a poetical appellation
				of Apollo as the god of light</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quae mihi Phoebus Apollo Praedixit,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					A. 3, 251</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Hor.
				C. S. 62</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Prop. 1, 2, 27</span></i>.—<b>Poet.</b> for <i>the sun</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dum rediens fugat astra Phoebus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hor.
					C. 3, 21, 24</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Phoebi pallidus orbis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. R. Am. 256</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">id. M. 2, 110</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tristior iccirco nox est, quam tempora Phoebi,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. R. Am. 585</span></i>
			.—Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Phoe-bēĭus</span></b> , a, um,
				adj., <i>Phœbean</i>, <i>Apollinean</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">juvenis,</span>”
				i. e. <i>Æsculapius</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Stat.
					S. 3, 4, 6</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">anguis,</span>”
				<i>of Æsculapius</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Ov.
					M. 15, 742</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ictus,</span>”
				<i>of the sun</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					ib. 5, 389</span></i>
			: ales, <i>the raven</i>, so called because
			metamorphosed by Apollo, <i><span class="en">Stat. S. 2, 4, 17</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">oscen,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Aus. Idyll. 11, 15</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Idmon,</span>”
				<i>son of Phœbus</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Val.
					Fl. 1, 228</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Circe,</span>”
				<i>daughter of Sol</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Petr. 135</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Phoe-bēus</span></b> , a,
				um, adj., <i>Phœbean</i>, <i>Apollinean</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">carmina,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Lucr.
					2, 504</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lampas,</span>”
				<i>the sun</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Verg. A.
					4, 6</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">virgo,</span>”
				<i>Daphne</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Ov.
					P. 2, 2, 82</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">laurus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Tr. 4, 2, 51</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Rhodos,</span>”
				<i>where the worship of Apollo prevailed</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">id. M.
					7, 365</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lyra,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					H. 16, 180</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sortes,</span>”
				<i>oracle</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">id. M.
					3, 130</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tripodes,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. A.
					A. 3, 789</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Phoebeā morbos pellere arte,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. F.
					3, 827</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>C.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Phoebas</span></b> ,
			ădis, f., <i>a
				priestess of Apollo;</i> hence <i>the inspired
			one</i>, <i>the prophetess</i>, <i><span class="en">Ov. Am. 2,
				8, 12</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Tr. 2, 400</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Luc. 5,
			128</span></i>; <i><span class="en">165</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
